    "answer": {
      "short": "$1002$, the smallest four-digit multiple of $6$.",
      "worked": "A number divisible by both $2$ and $3$ is divisible by $6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}166\\times6&=996\\\\167\\times6&=1002\\end{align*}$$\nThese are consecutive multiples of $6$, so the smallest four-digit number is $1002$.",
